**Rationale**: The 19 wt% / 5°C / 0s / N2 / 1500s condition is the best-confirmed Pareto candidate (~690 bar, 0.33 PF across two valid runs). This experiment introduces a 30s air exposure delay (vs. 0s) and a moderate pullcast speed (5 mm/s vs. 3 mm/s), both unexplored at this polymer/bath combination. A brief evaporation period can promote surface densification, potentially increasing modulus; the cold bath and N2 atmosphere are retained to preserve pore fraction. This is a genuinely new point adjacent to the confirmed best region, offering informative exploration of the modulus–pore fraction tradeoff without duplicating existing data.

