**Approximate Pareto front** (high modulus, high pore fraction simultaneously):
- High modulus / lower pore fraction: 17p5-20deg-90s-N2-1250s run2 (960, 0.27), 17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s run1 (937, 0.27)
- Balanced: 19-5deg-0s-N2-1500s run1 (768, 0.34), 20-5deg-150s-N2-1650s run1 (756, 0.34)
- High pore fraction / lower modulus: 17p5-19deg-90s-N2-1800s run4 (331, 0.44), 17p5-15deg-400s-NoN2-1800s (400, 0.40)

The **key gap** in the Pareto front is the region combining **modulus ~500–700 bar with pore fraction ≥ 0.36–0.40**. No experiment has achieved both simultaneously with good quality. The high-pore-fraction candidates (≥0.38) all have modulus below ~470 bar. The high-modulus candidates (≥700 bar) all have pore fraction ≤ 0.34.

### Validation Status Check

- **17p5-20deg-90s-N2-1250s**: runs 1, 2, 3, 5 exist. Run2 gave 960 bar / 0.27 (large SD=387, high CV), run3 gave 385 bar / 0.33, run5 gave 530 bar / 0.35. The run2 value is an outlier with very high SD — not reproducible. This candidate is not confirmed as a high-modulus point.
- **19-5deg-0s-N2-1500s**: runs 1, 3, 4, 5 exist. Run1: 768/0.34 (good quality), run3: 614/0.32 (wrinkles), run4: 890/0.29 (minor wrinkles, high SD=251), run5: 738/0.30 (wrinkles). The run1 result (768/0.34) is the best quality single measurement but the condition shows high variability across runs.
- **17p5-19deg-90s-N2-1800s run4**: 331/0.44 — only one run with good quality. This is a high-pore-fraction candidate that has not been independently validated.

### Strategy

The **17p5-19deg-90s-N2-1800s run4** result (Pore Fraction = 0.44, Modulus = 331 bar, good image quality) is the highest pore fraction observed with a clean membrane. It has only one valid measurement. Per the validation policy, this Pareto-front candidate (highest pore fraction, potentially Pareto-dominant over other high-PF candidates) should be validated before treating it as confirmed.

However, I also note that the **gap region** (modulus ~600–800 bar, pore fraction ~0.36–0.40) is unexplored. The condition `17p5-19deg-90s-N2-1800s` at bath_temp=19°C with N2 gave run4 (PF=0.44, good quality) but runs 1, 2, 3, 5 showed wrinkles and lower PF (0.27–0.36). The run4 result is anomalously high PF and may reflect measurement uncertainty.

Given the validation policy priority: **validate 17p5-19deg-90s-N2-1800s** (run4 conditions) since it is the highest pore fraction observed with good membrane quality and has not been independently reproduced.

Parameters: mixing_temp=65, bath_temp=19, pullcast_speed=10, nitrogen=true, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=90, nips_bath_wait_time=1800, polymer_wt=17.5, additive_wt=0.0.

**Expected benefit**: If the PF=0.44 result is reproducible, this would be a strong Pareto-front point (highest pore fraction in the dataset). If it regresses to ~0.27–0.36 (as in other runs), it clarifies that the run4 result was an outlier and we should search elsewhere for high-PF candidates. Either outcome is highly informative for the two-objective optimization.

